---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { PHONE, PHONE_TEL } from '../../lib/site.ts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Why hire us"
  description="Why pay for an independent foundation second opinion in Arizona? vs free inspections, vs repair-company surveys, vs engineering firms."
>
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="page-title">Why hire us</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      You're not paying for a verdict. You're paying for someone who completes the picture.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>vs. a free foundation inspection</h2>
      <p>
        Free evaluations are not free to perform. Someone pays — usually through repair volume and
        close rates. That doesn't make every recommendation wrong, but it can shape what gets
        emphasized and what gets less airtime: <em>monitor</em>, <em>this may never get worse</em>,
        <em>fix drainage first</em>.
      </p>
      <p>
        You hire us once. We don't need a repair contract to make the visit worthwhile.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>vs. a floor survey from a repair company</h2>
      <p>
        Many foundation repair companies can shoot floor elevations — sometimes for a fee, sometimes
        as part of a proposal visit. The measurement may be real. The next conversation is still
        usually about whether to buy a repair.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use professional leveling equipment and stop at advice. If repair is warranted, we'll say
        so — with credibility, because we have no stake in the steel. If it isn't, we'll say that
        too. Honest contractors benefit either way: you send them better-informed clients, and the
        right jobs still get done.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>vs. hiring an engineering firm first</h2>
      <p>
        Geotechnical and structural engineers do essential work — especially when design, stamps, or
        litigation matter. Many firms won't drive to Show Low for $1,250, and stamped reports cost
        more than a homeowner often needs on day one.
      </p>
      <p>
        We fill the gap: practical field measurement and honest guidance. When an Arizona PE is the
        right next step, we'll tell you plainly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What you're buying</h2>
      <table class="compare">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th></th>
            <th>Foundation Repair Advocate</th>
            <th>Typical sales visit</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Fee</td>
            <td>Paid upfront — clarity is the product</td>
            <td>"Free" — recovered through repair</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Goal</td>
            <td>Recommend a path — including repair when it's warranted</td>
            <td>Often toward a repair proposal</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>"Wait and monitor"</td>
            <td>Said when supported</td>
            <td>Rare</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Repair sold</td>
            <td>Never</td>
            <td>Core business</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          <strong>25 years in foundation repair and geotechnical field work.</strong> We translate
          what the industry knows into what homeowners deserve to hear — without talking over your
          head or under it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={`tel:${PHONE_TEL}`}>Talk it through — {PHONE}</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
